# local-only measurements/notes (never commit)
internal/
# E-7 (prompts/AGENT_QUEUE.md §HYGIENE-E7) — `internal/` above matches docs/internal/ too, so every NEW
# document written there since the rule landed has been SILENTLY UNTRACKED. The 84 that are tracked
# survive only because they were added before it (git keeps tracking a file it already knows), and
# docs/internal/ERP_COVERAGE_MATRIX.md — the headline scoreboard — is one of those: one accident away
# from being local-only. Markdown under docs/internal IS documentation, not a local measurement, so
# un-ignore it by name. The directory must be un-ignored first (git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded), then its contents re-excluded, then the .md re-included — so
# docs/internal/guidepics/ (≈5 MB of PNGs) and anything else non-markdown stays ignored exactly as now.
!docs/internal/
docs/internal/*
!docs/internal/*.md
build/erp/.demo_controller_key.json
/build/erp/shard_poc/
/build/erp/shards/*.db
/build/erp/post_poc/*.db

# Playwright/test-runner output (regenerated by test runs, not source)
/test-results/
/deploy/test-results/
/deploy/dev/test-results/

# Minified viewer bundle (generated by scripts/minify_viewer.sh, uploaded to OCI not committed)
/deploy/min/

# Raw pipeline input staging (large extraction DBs; canonical ignored copy lives under DAGCompiler/lib/)
/input/

# ── NO BINARY .db IN GIT — repo-wide, added 2026-09-01 with the LFS removal ────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md DB POLICY: binary .db commits are banned outright and unconditionally. The blanket
# `*.db filter=lfs` rule in .gitattributes had pulled 59 DBs (1.79 GB) into HEAD; they were
# untracked (files kept on disk) and every path they lived in is closed here so they cannot come
# back by accident. DB content reaches a consumer as migration/*.sql or <app>/patches/*.sql plus a
# self-heal loader; full rebuilt binaries go to OCI (deploy/OCI_UPLOAD.md §RULES). See
# prompts/LFS_QUOTA_AUDIT.md for the measurement this came from.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# The two SQL-defined exceptions stay tracked as TEXT, never as binaries:
!migration/*.sql
!**/patches/*.sql
